 "relevance_note": "One AOSD cohort patient carries a TNFAIP3 variant with individual-level detail: 'Patient 4 | TNFAIP3 (c.1939A>C) | Female, 60 years'.",
 "method_note": "Hand-built from Table 2 and the text; no table transcribed by script (a short script only assembled the JSON). Cohort of 24 AOSD patients tested by NGS; only Patient 4 (TNFAIP3 c.1939A>C, VUS) is in scope; the other four variant carriers (NOD2, TNFRSF1A, SCN9A) and the 19 others are out of scope. No relatives described. Protein 'T647P' is taken from Table 3 'Present study (2024)' column ('TNFAIP3: T647P'), the only TNFAIP3 variant in the study, so attributed to Patient 4; it is one-letter notation without 'p.' and is recorded as printed. Table 2 gives 'Female, 60 years' without saying whether 60 is age at diagnosis, onset or report, so all age fields are left not reported. Fever is reported without recurrence, so checklist 'recurrent fever' is left not reported (the Fever feature row is kept). 'Elevated acute-phase reactant levels' and 'hyperferritinemia' come from 'all patients had ...' (whole cohort, which includes Patient 4) and are marked inferred from group statement; mapped to checklist 'elevated inflammatory markers (CRP/ESR)'. Cohort-level counts (e.g. ANA positive n=2, lymphadenopathy 14/24) are not attributed to anyone. Discussion assigns this patient to cluster 2 ('uncomplicated' group) and says she 'did not show atypical symptoms'; not recorded as features. The Discussion spells the gene 'TNFAIP' once (typo). No contradictions found.",
